{"assets":[],"contestId":"432","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/432/problem/A"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"432A - Choosing Teams"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In this problem you should count number of students who can participate in ACM, divide it by 3 and round down. It could be done like this:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"int cnt = 0;\n\nfor(int i = 0; i < n; i++)\n    if (5 - a[i] >= k)\n        cnt++;\n\nint ans = cnt / 3;"},{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/432/problem/B"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"432B - Football Kit"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Count for every team number of games in home kit. For team "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" it equals to sum of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1 games at home and some away games with such teams which home kit color equals away kit color of team "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". To count number of such away games you could calc array "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cnt"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] — number of teams with home color kit "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". The solution could be implemented in this wasy:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"for(int i = 0; i < n; i++)\n    cnt[ x[i] ]++;\n\nfor(int i = 0; i < n; i++)\n{\n    ans_home[i] = n - 1;\n    ans_home[i] += cnt[ y[i] ];\n\n    ans_away[i] = 2 * (n - 1) - ans_home[i];\n}"},{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/432/problem/C"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"432C - Prime Swaps"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The solution can be described by pseudo-code:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":true},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Consider elements of permutation from 1 to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"While current element "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is not sutiated on position "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let the position of element "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" equals "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"pos"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Find maximum prime integer "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" which is less or equal than $pos — i + 1"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Swap element in positions "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"pos"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"pos"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 1"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It could be proved that such algorithm makes less than 4"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" swaps (for example, by implementing the algorithm)"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"This algorithm should be implemented optimally. You should maintain positions of elements of permutation. Swap function in author's solution: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"void doSwap(int i, int j){\n    int x = a[i], y = a[j];\n    a[j] = x, pos[x] = j;\n    a[i] = y, pos[y] = i;\n    result.push_back(make_pair(i, j));\n}"},{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/432/problem/D"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"432D - Prefixes and Suffixes"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The problem could be solved using different algorithms with z and prefix functions. Let's describe the solution with prefix function "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" of string "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"line_break"},{"kind":"text","text":"Calc prefix function and create a tree where vertices — integers from 0 to |"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"|, edges — from "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" for every "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". The root of the tree is 0. For every vertex "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" calc the number of values "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] = "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" — that is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cnt"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"]. Then for every "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" calc the sum all values "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cnt"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"u"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] for every "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"u"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" in to subtree of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The general answer to the problem is:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Find all lenghts of the prefixes which matches the suffixes — these values are |"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"|, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"[|"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"|], "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"[|"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"|]], "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"[|"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"|]]]... For every such length "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"L"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" the answer to the problem is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"sum"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"L"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] + 1."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/432/problem/E"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"432E - Square Tiling"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"This is popular test 6 :)"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"13 5\n\nAAAAA\nAAAAA\nAAAAA\nAAAAA\nAAAAA\nBBBBB\nBBBBB\nBBBBB\nBBBBB\nBBBBB\nAAACA\nAAABB\nAAABB"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The problem could be solved in a standard way — try to fill the table from the first cell to the last and try to put the miminum letter."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Consider the first row. Obviously it begins from some letters A (to be exact "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"min"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") letters A). When we put some letters A in the first row, we should put several letters A in some next rows to make a square. The next letter could be only B."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Describe the solution in general. Assume that we have already considered some rows. Consider row "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". Some cells in this row could be already painted. Consider unpainted cells from left to the right. For every such cell consider its color from A to Z. Two cases should be considered:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":true},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Put in this cell the minimum possible letter (neighbours have no such letter)"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If the previous cell in this row was not painted at the beginning of considering row "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", now it is already painted. We should try to merge the current cell with the square of the previous cell."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Choose the best case from these cases. Try to get the answer on test "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 13 "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 5 to understand the algorithm better."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"document"},"schema":2,"sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/blog/entry/12310"}